            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The grave, physical tomb, or the general realm of the dead (Sheol or Hades) where Jesus remained between his crucifixion and resurrection.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Matthew 12:40\",\"Jonah 2:2\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A specific spiritual region of the underworld or Hell, associated with Christ's active descent to the dead (the Harrowing of Hell).\",\"basis\":[\"Ephesians 4:9\",\"1 Peter 3:18-19\",\"Acts 2:27\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The grip of earthly authorities or the suffering of Jesus at the hands of the world, often geographically centered in Jerusalem.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 12:40\",\"Ezekiel 5:5\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The phrase is famously used by Jesus in Matthew 12:40 to describe the 'Sign of Jonah.' While the consensus overwhelmingly associates it with the three days of Christ's death and burial, denominational traditions diverge on whether it refers strictly to the physical grave or implies a literal descent into the spiritual underworld.\"}",
